config MTK_CONSYS_GPS
	bool "MediaTek MT6853 consys GNSS (/dev/stpgps, gps_emi, gps_pwr)"
	depends on MTK_CONSYS_WMT
	default n
	help
	  The /dev/stpgps character device used by the vendor mnld GNSS
	  daemon: the GNSS data stream carried over the WMT/STP core. The
	  GNSS function is powered through WMT on the first open and powered
	  down again on the last close. Nothing happens at boot.

	  /dev/gps_emi maps the GNSS window of the consys reserved EMI for
	  mnld and /dev/gps_pwr reports the connsys low-battery level.

	  The node is only created once the vendor wmt_loader has initialised
	  the connectivity drivers. mtk_stpgps.enable=0 on the kernel command
	  line keeps the node from being created.

	  If unsure, say N.
